    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG Thornton Properties are delighted to present this detached two-bedroom cottage to the market, set on a mature site extending to just over half an acre in a scenic countryside setting close to Avoca village.\n\nThe property offers a traditional cottage layout, with accommodation comprising a living room, dining room, kitchen and bathroom at ground floor level, with two bedrooms positioned on the first floor. The cottage is in need of refurbishment and is currently without services. Purchasers should note that a well and septic tank will need to be installed, subject to the necessary consents, and the property is therefore suitable for cash purchasers only.\n\nOutside, the grounds are a real feature of the property. Extending to just over half an acre, the site is mature and sloping, with established trees and informal garden areas offering considerable scope for clearance, landscaping and improvement.\n\nWhile requiring investment, the property retains traditional cottage character, including fireplaces, timber ceiling detail and a peaceful rural setting. For purchasers seeking a countryside project with land, privacy and long-term potential, this is an opportunity to restore and shape a home to their own requirements.\n\nLocated close to Avoca village, the property is well placed to enjoy the surrounding countryside while remaining within reach of local amenities, Arklow, Wicklow Town and the M11."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nLiving Room - 4.25m x 3.90m\nMain reception room with front-facing window, exposed timber ceiling, and feature fireplace with tiled surround. The front door opens directly into this room, which retains a traditional cottage feel and provides access through to the rear of the property.\n\nDining Room - 4.25m x 2.83m\nSecond reception room with front-facing window, timber ceiling joists, and decorative fireplace. A useful additional living space offering scope for use as a dining room, sitting room or as part of any future reconfiguration.\n\nKitchen - 1.60m x 2.13m\nCompact kitchen positioned to the rear of the property, accessed from the living room.\n\nBathroom - 1.60m x 2.44m\nGround floor bathroom fitted with bath, WC and wash hand basin, with dual-aspect windows providing natural light.\n\nLanding - 1.40m x 1.42m\nFirst floor landing providing access to both bedrooms.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.38m x 3.90m\nFirst floor double bedroom with timber panelled ceiling, timber floorboards and window overlooking the surrounding greenery.\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.25m x 2.79m\nDouble bedroom with timber panelled ceiling, timber floorboards, feature chimney breast and window enjoying an elevated countryside outlook.\n\n"
      },
      {
